checks.evidence:
tick():
  if (mInFlight != null || mTimeline == null) { return false; }
  long nowMs = mClock.elapsedRealtimeMs();
  if (nowMs - mLastStartMs < MIN_START_INTERVAL_MS) { return false; }
  if (nowMs < mCooldownUntilMs) { return false; }
  ... mInFlight = batch; mLastStartMs = nowMs; mInFlightCall = mService.translate(...)
Tests: startsAtMostOneCallAtATime (a second tick after 5 s with the first still in flight returns false and startCount stays 1); respectsTheMinimumStartInterval (999 ms refused, 1000 ms allowed).

cancel(): if (mInFlightCall != null) { mInFlightCall.cancel(); mCancelled = true; }
handleSuccess(): if (batch != mInFlight) return; boolean cancelled = mCancelled; release(); if (cancelled) return;
handleFailure(): same abandoned check before recording attempts.
Test: cancelledCallBlocksTheSlotUntilItReportsBack asserts the cancelled call blocks the slot (startCount stays 1), and that after the cancelled call reports a late success the cache stays empty and the slot is free.
